course: dictionary
lesson: 12488
title: One word, many meanings: demon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and demon is a good example. Read the words around it to find the right meaning, just as you do with any word you are not sure of.
explain: «In the Bible story, Jesus drove the demons out of the man.» The clues are Bible and drove out. Here demon means an evil spirit. Christians believe demons are fallen angels who oppose God.
explain: «In the game, the demon chased the hero through the dark castle.» The clues are game, dark castle and chased. Here demon means a wicked monster or spirit from a myth, legend or game.
explain: «Ella is a demon at maths.» No evil is meant here. Demon is informal talk for someone who does something with great energy or skill. Ask yourself: does the sentence sound frightening, or does it praise someone? Praise means the skill meaning.
fact: A demon is an evil spirit, as in Bible stories and church teaching.
fact: Christians believe demons are fallen angels who oppose God.
fact: In myths, legends and games, a demon is a wicked monster or spirit.
fact: Informal talk: «a speed demon» is someone who drives very fast, and «a demon at chess» is someone very skilled.
fact: Demons can also mean a person's inner troubles or bad memories, as in «fighting your demons».
exercise: «The knight fought the demon at the gates of the dark castle.» What is the demon in this story? | A kind helper who guards the castle | A knight who lost his sword | A very slow snail | *A wicked monster from a legend
exercise: «Ella is a demon at maths; she solves every puzzle in seconds.» What does demon mean here? | A sleepy dog | *A person who is very skilled | Someone who is always late | A wicked spirit
exercise: «Sam said he was fighting his demons after the bad news.» What does fighting his demons mean? | Playing a fight game | *Battling worries or bad memories | Running a race on the playground | Shouting at a teacher
test: In the Bible story, Jesus drove demons out of a man. What kind of demon is this? | A speed demon on a race track | *An evil spirit in a religious story | A small bird that sings at night | A kind teacher at the school
test: «Max drives like a speed demon on the motorway.» What does speed demon mean? | A road sign about traffic | *Someone who drives very fast | A slow and careful driver | A monster that lives under bridges
exam: Which sentence uses demon to mean a wicked monster in a game? | «The demon at chess won every game in the club.» | «The speed demon zoomed past the bus.» | «Ella fought her demons before the test.» | *«The demon in the game guarded the golden gate.»
